WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:03.260
I'm Angry…

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:05.760
with all of YOU!

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:06.760
Because you didn't go see

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:08.750
a lot of the best movies of the year!

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:09.750
But you can play catch-up

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:11.460
thanks to my list of the

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:14.820
Top 10 Most Underrated Movies of 2014

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:18.340
on this week's episode of Angry Nerd!

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:20.430
Okay, everyone agrees that television is in
the middle

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:22.880
of a golden age, or platinum age,

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:24.210
...or dilithium age...

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:25.210
...or whatever.

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:28.359
There all these terrific, compelling, challenging
series

00:00:28.359 --> 00:00:31.960
from HBO, AMC, Showtime, Netflix, Amazon...

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:34.290
But feature-length movies that play in theaters

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:36.270
are actually still pretty good,

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:37.470
IF you know where to look.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.410
Which, come to think of it,

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:41.730
will probably be your TV screen at this point.

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:44.120
Oh well, here are ten overlooked films

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:45.930
that truly deserve your attention.

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:47.100
Jim Jarmusch's flick

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.390
was the most compelling depiction of vampires

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:51.120
I've seen in years.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:53.220
I mean c’mon, If Dracula was real,

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:54.220
he wouldn't be

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:55.220
a blockbuster action hero

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:56.850
laying waste to rival armies,

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:59.330
or a sparkly teen heart throb

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:00.330
canoodling with

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:02.690
a twitchy wooden actress.

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:05.260
He would waste his days lounging around

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:07.219
and sucking on gourmet bloodsicles

00:01:07.219 --> 00:01:10.439
like the decadent Eurotrash that he is.

00:01:10.439 --> 00:01:13.049
This half-live action, half-animated

00:01:13.049 --> 00:01:16.869
adaptation of Stanislaw Lem's classic sci-fi
satire

00:01:16.869 --> 00:01:20.060
is the easily the most mind bending film of
the year.

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:21.219
Robin Wright is terrific

00:01:21.219 --> 00:01:24.240
as an actress who sells her likeness rights
to Hollywood

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:26.189
and then crosses over

00:01:26.189 --> 00:01:29.840
into a strange, hallucinogenic alternate universe.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:31.979
It's like Ralph Bakshi's Cool World..

00:01:31.979 --> 00:01:33.770
if Ralph Bakshi's Cool World

00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:36.299
was NOT absolutely terrible!

00:01:36.299 --> 00:01:37.390
Now, you'd hardly know it

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:38.429
from the ad campaign,

00:01:38.429 --> 00:01:40.190
but this clever no-budget dramedy

00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:44.409
about two couples and their...UNUSUAL relationship
issues

00:01:44.409 --> 00:01:48.649
has a HUGE sci-fi twist.

00:01:48.649 --> 00:01:50.310
Saying more would spoil it.

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:52.780
Just, just be sure to seek it out.

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:54.130
What a relief to see an action movie

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:56.619
with almost no plot

00:01:56.619 --> 00:01:57.619
or dialogue

00:01:57.619 --> 00:01:58.619
or special effects

00:01:58.619 --> 00:02:00.159
to distract from the action.

00:02:00.159 --> 00:02:02.539
BONUS: Google around to find a video

00:02:02.539 --> 00:02:05.009
of director Gareth Evans discussing his

00:02:05.009 --> 00:02:07.560
top five favorite fight scenes of all time.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.619
His list is one of my Top Five...

00:02:09.619 --> 00:02:10.740
Top...

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:13.000
Five lists!

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:14.800
Stephen Chow is like a cross between

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.720
Jackie Chan and Peter Jackson:

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:20.020
a master of slapstick comedy, martial arts,

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:21.560
AND digital effects.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:24.640
He's been all-but-ignored stateside since
Kung Fu Hustle,

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:28.500
but this adaptation of a classic 16th-century
Chinese novel

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:30.220
is worth tracking down.

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:33.460
The greatest sci fi flick of the 1970s was…

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:35.180
...never actually…

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:36.180
...filmed.

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:38.420
Cult director Alejandro Jodorowsky's

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:40.970
planned adaptation of Frank Herbert's novel
Dune

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:43.220
collapsed under the weight of its own ambitions

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:45.350
before it made it off of the drawing board.

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:47.650
But the sketchy outline that survives,

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:50.660
which is lovingly presented in this new documentary,

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:52.590
captures the imagination in ways

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:56.250
that few actual produced sci-fi flicks do.

00:02:56.250 --> 00:03:00.400
A South Korean adaptation of a French science
fiction comic

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.170
starring Captain America?!

00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:03.170
Sold!

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:05.880
Its depiction of a class war aboard a high
tech train

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:07.670
rocketing around a ruined earth

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:09.990
is as thought-provoking as it is thrilling.

00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:11.870
This film made a bundle overseas,

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:13.470
but it bombed stateside.

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:16.770
What is WRONG with us, America?!

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:19.310
This satire of romcom cliches starring

00:03:19.310 --> 00:03:20.950
Amy Poehler and Paul Rudd

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:23.130
was a hoot.

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:24.890
Some griped that it arrived too late

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:27.670
to really skewer its source material.

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:28.670
Seriously?!

00:03:28.670 --> 00:03:30.280
That's like saying that Wet Hot American Summer

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:32.530
is a failure because it was released

00:03:32.530 --> 00:03:34.850
two decades after Meatballs!

00:03:34.850 --> 00:03:37.530
Hayao Miyazaki is great and all,

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:42.550
but Isao Takahata is the unsung anime genius
of Studio Ghibili.

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:44.080
The director's newest release,

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:46.270
an adaptation of a Japanese folk tale,

00:03:46.270 --> 00:03:47.840
came and went from theaters.

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:50.190
But it ranks right up there with his classics

00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:53.560
like Pom Poko and Grave of the Fireflies

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:55.750
Let's pour one out for Live Die Repeat,

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:58.830
the Tom Cruise movie formerly known as

00:03:58.830 --> 00:03:59.860
Edge of Tomorrow.

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:04.100
Doug Liman's terrific adaptation of the clever
Japanese scifi novel

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:07.290
was the best blockbuster of the year,

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:09.540
and it should've been a HUGE hit.

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:13.950
But it bombed so terribly that the studio
renamed it for the DVD release…

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:18.959
...the way its protagonist continually gets
to relive the last 48 hours

00:04:18.959 --> 00:04:20.799
over and over again.

00:04:20.799 --> 00:04:24.289
This is a Tom Cruise movie that even Tom Cruise
haters can love!

00:04:24.289 --> 00:04:27.150
Thanks to the Groundhog Day-style story structure,

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:28.930
you get to see him die

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:30.740
dozens and dozens of times.

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:31.930
I stand by everything

00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:34.420
I said about it at the time of its release--

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:37.500
it's the best movie ever made about video
games,

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:40.199
EVEN THOUGH it's not about video games.

00:04:40.199 --> 00:04:42.550
Hmmm, maybe I'll go back in time

00:04:42.550 --> 00:04:45.870
and warn the studio not to give it such a
lame title!

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:51.099
AND I'll also warn myself not to eat that
ceviche from 7-11…

00:04:51.099 --> 00:04:53.650
[time rewind noise]

00:04:53.650 --> 00:04:57.379
By the way, I HATE top 10 lists!

00:04:57.379 --> 00:04:59.100
It's such an arbitrary limitation!

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:03.659
I wish it was a top 67 list, so I could've
included:

00:05:03.659 --> 00:05:08.430
Cooties, Open Windows, The Rover, Enemy,

00:05:08.430 --> 00:05:13.289
The Double, Zero Theorem, Automata, Blue Ruin,

00:05:13.289 --> 00:05:17.849
Coherence, Stretch, The Babadook, Under the
Skin,

00:05:17.849 --> 00:05:19.620
The Vanquishing of the Witch Baba Yaga--

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:20.620
HEY!

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:21.620
DON'T FADE OUT!

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:22.620
I'M NOT DONE YET!

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:23.969
A Most Wanted Man, To Be Takei,

00:05:23.969 --> 00:05:26.770
The Galapagos Affair, Alan Partridge...

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:27.770
What do you think is

00:05:27.770 --> 00:05:30.289
the most underrated movie of 2014?

00:05:30.289 --> 00:05:31.289
Let me know in the comments

00:05:31.289 --> 00:05:32.590
and click down here to subscribe

00:05:32.590 --> 00:05:34.090
for more Angry Nerd.

